#EXTM3U
# A playlist of public test streams, so MoPlayer can be launched, driven and
# demonstrated without anyone's real IPTV credentials.
#
#   moplayer asset://demo.m3u
#
# (asset://demo.m3u is the shipped form — it loads THIS file out of the app's
# own bundle, so it works from the installed /usr/lib/moplayer, not only from a
# source checkout. A bare `moplayer assets/demo.m3u` still works when run from
# this source tree.)
#
# These are HLS and MPEG-TS from public test rigs — the same two containers a
# real Xtream panel serves — so this exercises the real playback path, not a mock
# of it.
#
# No commas in the channel names. `#EXTINF` ends its attribute list at the first
# comma and calls everything after it the name, so "Sintel (HLS, multi-audio)"
# arrives as a channel called "multi-audio)". Every M3U parser in existence has
# this hole; the fix is in the playlist, not the parser.

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="bbb" tvg-logo="https://image.mux.com/VZtzUzGRv02OhRnZCxcNg49OilvolTqdnFLEqBsTwaxU/thumbnail.png" group-title="Test Streams",Big Buck Bunny
https://test-streams.mux.dev/x36xhzz/x36xhzz.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="sintel" group-title="Test Streams",Sintel — multi-audio HLS
https://bitdash-a.akamaihd.net/content/sintel/hls/playlist.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="apple-basic" group-title="Test Streams",Apple BipBop — fMP4 HLS
https://devstreaming-cdn.apple.com/videos/streaming/examples/img_bipbop_adv_example_fmp4/master.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="nasa" group-title="Live",NASA TV Public
https://ntv1.akamaized.net/hls/live/2014075/NASA-NTV1-HLS/master.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="tears" group-title="Live",Tears of Steel
https://test-streams.mux.dev/pts_shift/master.m3u8
